# Standalone orchestrator image — environment template.
#
# The orchestrator image runs a whole `tolokaforge run` batch (NOT the
# single-trial driver in deploy/standalone/). Copy this file to `.env`, fill in
# the provider key your task's models route to, and mount it read-only into the
# container — the one-command wrapper does this for you:
#
#   cp deploy/orchestrator/.env.example .env
#   scripts/docker/run-orchestrator.sh -c path/to/run_config.yaml -e .env
#
# The wrapper mounts this file at /work/.env, where the engine's SecretManager
# reads it via DotEnvProvider. It is never baked into the image, never passed as
# a build-arg. A keyless `--dry-run` needs no `.env` at all. Keep this an
# EXAMPLE: put no real secrets here.
#
# See docs/ORCHESTRATOR_IMAGE.md for the full walkthrough.

# --- LLM provider credentials -------------------------------------------------
# Set the key for the provider your task's models route to. OpenRouter is the
# common default; the sibling keys cover direct-provider routing. A task whose
# grading declares `llm_judge` needs the provider key its judge model routes to
# (typically OPENROUTER_API_KEY).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
